MID_EV11_072_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_072_m01_001: Listen up! Incoming Anna administrative\nannouncement for the Heroic Games!
MID_EV11_072_m01_002: Congratulations to Ribeira Winds for winning the\nfirst match in the qualifiers!
MID_EV11_072_m01_003: Thanks, Anna!
MID_EV11_072_m01_004: I got to see your latest match too. You didn't yield a\nsingle inch to those grown-ups.
MID_EV11_072_m01_005: Here I was worried about you being kids, but you\nknow how to get the job done.
MID_EV11_072_m01_006: W-well, I guess. Heh... I'm a little embarrassed to\nget a compliment like that.
MID_EV11_072_m01_007: Haha! Well, I'll be rooting for you in the next round,\nso you better give it everything you've got.
MID_EV11_072_m01_008: Moving on! We've set a date for your next match,\nand I'm here to give you the news.
MID_EV11_072_m01_009: The details are written down here, so take a\ngood look.
MID_EV11_072_m01_010: <TLP>Ribeira Winds\n\nMatch: Second Qualifier of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Thundercloud Knights\nLeader: Benditz\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}
MID_EV11_072_m01_011: So what do you think? Are you getting used to\nfighting in the arena?
MID_EV11_072_m01_012: I'm surprised by how much the arena changes.\nThey even reshape the terrain.
MID_EV11_072_m01_013: The whole layout changes for each battle, so our\ntactics need to change too.
MID_EV11_072_m01_014: I'm still adjusting to how many people are watching.
MID_EV11_072_m01_015: I can't stop thinking about all those strangers staring\nat us.
MID_EV11_072_m01_016: That doesn't really change how I fight.
MID_EV11_072_m01_017: Never thought I'd be fighting next to\nTheodora, though.
MID_EV11_072_m01_018: You're on a first-name basis with a queen?\nI'm impressed.
MID_EV11_072_m01_019: Your next opponent is more, uh, quirky than most\nyou've seen so far, so be ready.
MID_EV11_077_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_077_m01_001: Hello! Hey! You there!
MID_EV11_077_m01_002: Who, me?
MID_EV11_077_m01_003: You're one of the fighters in the Heroic Games,\naren't you?
MID_EV11_077_m01_004: I am! Looks like it's made me kind of famous.
MID_EV11_077_m01_005: My name is Aswan. I was hoping I'd run into a\nfighter if I waited here.
MID_EV11_077_m01_023: <NCA>Give her your name.
MID_EV11_077_m01_008: I'm Cai from Ribeira village. Is there something I\ncan help you with, Aswan?
MID_EV11_077_m01_009: I've heard that some fighters have access to\ndifferent facilities in and around the arena.
MID_EV11_077_m01_010: I've also heard that fighters can get into places that\nare off-limits to the general public.
MID_EV11_077_m01_011: Since you're involved with the games, it's fortuitous\nthat I met you, Cai from Ribeira village.
MID_EV11_077_m01_012: I'd like to beg a favor of you, Cai.
MID_EV11_077_m01_013: Could I perhaps accompany you into the dungeon\nthat people say sits beneath the arena?
MID_EV11_077_m01_014: Why would you want to go down there?
MID_EV11_077_m01_015: It's very important that I meet with the White-\nManed Demon.
MID_EV11_077_m01_016: I have something I must give him.
MID_EV11_077_m01_017: W-well, the thing about the dungeon is...they don't\nusually even let fighters from the games in.
MID_EV11_077_m01_018: Yes, but I understand you've already been in to meet\nwith the White-Maned Demon.
MID_EV11_077_m01_019: And I also understand that you've been learning\nweapon arts from him directly. I'm right, aren't I?
MID_EV11_077_m01_020: How do you know about that?
MID_EV11_077_m01_021: Hehe! In your match the other day, I saw your\nmoves, and I had no doubts as to their origins.
MID_EV11_077_m01_022: I guess you got me. There's more to you than you let\non isn't there, Aswan?
MID_EV11_078_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_078_m01_001: Here we are, Aswan.
MID_EV11_078_m01_002: Bertrand!
MID_EV11_078_m01_004: Aswan?! How did you get in here?
MID_EV11_078_m01_005: I thought... I thought I'd never see you again!
MID_EV11_078_m01_006: Ever since that day, I've wished I could apologize...
MID_EV11_078_m01_008: I should have trusted you. Why didn't I?
MID_EV11_078_m01_009: But...one can't change the past. At least now, I can\ntell you I'm sorry.
MID_EV11_078_m01_010: I hope you'll forgive me.
MID_EV11_078_m01_011: Please. How could you have known the full,\nawful truth of it?
MID_EV11_078_m01_012: I certainly didn't.
MID_EV11_078_m01_013: I have no doubt, now, of your innocence.
MID_EV11_078_m01_014: Aswan... It was a surprise to see you at that match.
MID_EV11_078_m01_016: I'd held on so long to the dream, the promise,\nof returning to you. It was what kept me fighting.
MID_EV11_078_m01_017: And it still is. I swear I will survive the trial Mars \nhas given me and return to your side.
MID_EV11_078_m01_018: I know better than to doubt you anymore.
MID_EV11_078_m01_019: Bertrand, I want you to have this.
MID_EV11_078_m01_020: An axe? But...impossible!
MID_EV11_078_m01_021: The Aragonian royal family's treasure, the Bloodaxe.\nOnce wielded by King Hanno, it's said.
MID_EV11_078_m01_022: When I heard rumors of the White-Maned Demon of\nthe Arena, I realized you might still be alive.
MID_EV11_078_m01_023: I thought I could do something to help you, even if it\nwas only a little. So I took it, in secret.
MID_EV11_078_m01_024: Because you're innocent, the souls of past kings—\nincluding my father—will come to your aid.
MID_EV11_078_m01_025: Aswan, with this, I'll have the strength of a hundred\nmen. I'm truly in your debt.
MID_EV11_078_m01_026: That's...the queen of Arago? What is she doing here?
MID_EV11_078_m01_027: And that axe... It can't be... Oh my. This is getting\nvery interesting.
MID_EV11_078_m01_028: We'll keep this secret from our sisters, right, Babbu?
MID_EV11_078_m01_029: I think I've seen that axe somewhere before...\nWhy would I have that feeling?
MID_EV11_078_m01_039: 
MID_EV11_078_m01_030: Oh! In my dream, the woman I saw was holding it.
MID_EV11_078_m01_031: Cai? What's the matter?
MID_EV11_078_m01_032: I think I'm imagining things. I'm fine. Don't worry.
MID_EV11_078_m01_033: But listen... Adults are a mystery to me.
MID_EV11_078_m01_034: Is Aswan...the reason you need to return home?
MID_EV11_078_m01_035: Yes. More or less...
MID_EV11_078_m01_036: I have so many questions, but I think I should leave\nyou two alone to talk for a while.
MID_EV11_078_m01_037: Just call me when you need me. Don't take too long,\nand don't make trouble for Gabriel, OK?
MID_EV11_078_m01_038: Sure. We'll keep that in mind.
MID_EV11_029_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_029_m01_001: Uh-oh. I think everyone else is here. Looks like\nwe're the last ones to arrive.
MID_EV11_029_m01_050: 
MID_EV11_029_m01_051: 
MID_EV11_029_m01_052: 
MID_EV11_029_m01_002: Hey, look, it's the Mystery Bride. She's already\nreally famous in Dagsion.
MID_EV11_029_m01_003: She's super strong, and her fortune-telling is accurate.\nThere's always a line of customers at her stall.
MID_EV11_029_m01_037: Hey, look, it's the Mystery Bride. She's already\nreally famous in Dagsion.
MID_EV11_029_m01_038: She's super strong, and her fortune-telling is accurate.\nThere's always a line of customers at her stall.
MID_EV11_029_m01_004: That man with the long hair... I don't think I've seen\nsomeone so beautiful.
MID_EV11_029_m01_005: And what's going on over there? An argument?
MID_EV11_029_m01_006: Fate has reunited us—and here, of all places. A\nstrange phenomenon, is it not?
MID_EV11_029_m01_007: I have nothing to say to you.
MID_EV11_029_m01_008: Can you please keep your distance from her,\nMr. Anacharsis of Agartha?
MID_EV11_029_m01_009: That's more of a command than a request.\nTrust me—it's for your own good.
MID_EV11_029_m01_010: It would seem that you despise me no mean amount.\nIf that is how it's to be, then so it shall be.
MID_EV11_029_m01_011: Uh, hi. I'm Cai. Looking forward to working with\nyou today.
MID_EV11_029_m01_012: Ah.
MID_EV11_029_m01_013: Did I say something wrong?
MID_EV11_029_m01_014: Hm? So rude. Don't pay attention to him, Cai.
MID_EV11_029_m01_015: "Ignore rude people, no matter how good they look."\nThat's what Grandpa says. Well, something like that.
MID_EV11_029_m01_016: Sorry about that. Sweetie is...not exactly a people\nperson, if you know what I mean.
MID_EV11_029_m01_017: Until you get to know him, there might be a\nmisunderstanding or two. But I wouldn't worry.
MID_EV11_029_m01_018: Anyway, I'm Esmeralda, and Sweetie's really\ncalled Dietrich.
MID_EV11_029_m01_019: This big, unfriendly looking weirdo is Fabio.
MID_EV11_029_m01_020: Must you chatter even now? Please, leave me out\nof it.
MID_EV11_029_m01_021: But don't get the idea that Sweetie is all bad. He\nsaved me!
MID_EV11_029_m01_022: Really? He likes helping people too?
MID_EV11_029_m01_023: I mean, don't go thinking he's a good person or\nanything. He can be pretty cruel.
MID_EV11_029_m01_039: Sorry about that. Sweetie is...not exactly a people\nperson, if you know what I mean.
MID_EV11_029_m01_040: Until you get to know him, there might be a\nmisunderstanding or two. But I wouldn't worry.
MID_EV11_029_m01_041: Anyway, I'm Esmeralda, and Sweetie's really\ncalled Dietrich.
MID_EV11_029_m01_042: This big, unfriendly looking weirdo is Fabio.
MID_EV11_029_m01_043: Must you chatter even now? Please, leave me out\nof it.
MID_EV11_029_m01_044: But don't get the idea that Sweetie is all bad. He\nsaved me!
MID_EV11_029_m01_045: Really? He likes helping people too?
MID_EV11_029_m01_046: I mean, don't go thinking he's a good person or\nanything. He can be pretty cruel.
MID_EV11_029_m01_053: 
MID_EV11_029_m01_024: Kids fighting in arena matches? Pretty impressive.
MID_EV11_029_m01_025: But, um, are you gonna be OK? I bet your parents are\nworried sick about you...
MID_EV11_029_m01_026: Parents... Ugh, I'm so homesick...
MID_EV11_029_m01_047: Kids fighting in arena matches? Pretty impressive.
MID_EV11_029_m01_048: But, um, are you gonna be OK? I bet your parents are\nworried sick about you...
MID_EV11_029_m01_049: Parents... Ugh, I'm so homesick...
MID_EV11_029_m01_028: Cai, was it?
MID_EV11_029_m01_029: You have it too, don't you? Strength akin to\nTheodora's and Bahr Vahn's.
MID_EV11_029_m01_030: Incredible strength that brings with it a curse.\nDrake's treasures... It's so mysterious.
MID_EV11_029_m01_031: It's not spirit magic, and yet it's also different from\nthe power of Vritra's followers.
MID_EV11_029_m01_033: If I had to quantify it, I'd say it's similar to the power\nwielded by temple adherents.
MID_EV11_029_m01_034: Are you talking about sacred magic?
MID_EV11_029_m01_035: I dunno. Doesn't really feel that way to me.
MID_EV11_029_m01_036: Many wielding this power have been brought\ntogether in the games. It's all very strange...
MID_EV11_076_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_076_m01_001: Let us look back, over 16 hundred years into the\npast! Has our astute audience already figured it out?
MID_EV11_076_m01_002: Today we recreate a legendary battle that predates\nthe existence of the Dagdan Imperial Calendar.
MID_EV11_076_m01_003: This most important event laid the foundations for\nDagda the Great's pacification of wild lands.
MID_EV11_076_m01_004: I speak of course of the Battle of Tarvos!
MID_EV11_076_m01_005: Mysterious Iskandariya ruled the desert with an iron\nfist for more than a millennium.
MID_EV11_076_m01_006: Contesting supremacy over this land, our Dagdan\nEmpire clashed with her foes at Tarvos!
MID_EV11_076_m01_007: In the east—Benditz, head of the Thundercloud\nKnights, leads the Iskandariyan charioteers!
MID_EV11_076_m01_008: In the west—strong and fetching fighters from many\nlands make up our elite Dagdan forces!
MID_EV11_076_m01_009: Quiver with anticipation, onlookers, for our epic\nbattle is about to begin!
MID_EV11_076_m01_010: Look at this place! It's downright majestic. I can't\nwait to bask in my victory on this battlefield.
MID_EV11_076_m01_011: How the mediocre do love to build themselves up—\nthe same puffery all barbarians spew.
MID_EV11_076_m01_012: But tell me what you think. I imagine you may well\nhave more in common with the man than I.
MID_EV11_076_m01_013: Those who lack confidence bray the loudest. Self-\ndoubt leaks through the mouth.
MID_EV11_076_m01_014: It is a sad attempt to project confidence yet no\ndifferent than if he had yelled, "you terrify me!"
MID_EV11_076_m01_015: I see. But are you not like him when you cackle your\nway through your foes?
MID_EV11_076_m01_016: I am not boasting. That is my sincere reaction to the\nrevelry of battle.
MID_EV11_076_m01_017: These foes seem trifling, insignificant. I do not expect\nto derive much joy from this.
MID_EV11_076_m01_018: I've gained yet another resource for understanding\nthe composition of your character.
MID_EV11_076_m01_019: I have a proposal, if I may. Perhaps we ought to call\na truce and cooperate for now.
MID_EV11_076_m01_020: Do not address me, follower of Vritra.
MID_EV11_076_m01_021: Shouldn't victory come first? I believe our interests\nare in alignment.
MID_EV11_076_m01_022: I said, do not address me. Consider yourself warned.
MID_EV11_076_m01_023: Um, Fabio... You're not having the best day here,\nare you?
MID_EV11_076_m01_024: Your concern is unneeded.
MID_EV11_076_m01_025: You say that, but you actually look out for some\npeople quite a bit, don't you?
MID_EV11_076_m01_026: Even if you don't realize you're doing it.
MID_EV11_076_m01_027: Your observations and appraisals are unwarranted.
MID_EV11_076_m01_028: I was expecting a challenge, but this group's a mess.\nGood luck tryin' to work as a team.
MID_EV11_076_m01_029: You're unruly, untrained... Hahaha! This'll be easy.
MID_EV11_076_m01_030: Doesn't matter how strong each of you are on your\nown. You're gonna learn that the hard way.
MID_EV11_076_m01_031: Well, that and what it feels like to lose to me and\nmy troops.
MID_EV11_076_m01_032: There's something about the enemy's formation...\nYes! I knew I wasn't imagining it!
MID_EV11_076_m01_033: It's identical to that of the Third Division of Arago...\nThat's the elite branch of their regular army!
MID_EV11_030_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_030_m01_002: E-excuse me, Dietrich? I'd like to thank you for what\nyou did.
MID_EV11_030_m01_046: 
MID_EV11_030_m01_047: 
MID_EV11_030_m01_048: 
MID_EV11_030_m01_003: Your gratitude is unnecessary. My blade was in\nreach. That is all.
MID_EV11_030_m01_001: I... Every battle, I think I'm going to die...
MID_EV11_030_m01_044: But I'm just glad that Tialla's safe and sound.
MID_EV11_030_m01_032: I... Every battle, I think I'm going to die...
MID_EV11_030_m01_045: But I'm just glad that Tialla's safe and sound.
MID_EV11_030_m01_004: Dietrich, that sword isn't a normal sword, right?
MID_EV11_030_m01_005: It is the fell blade Answerer, known as a Hero's Relic.
MID_EV11_030_m01_006: It is the legacy of my forebears passed to me in\nFódlan. A blade to smite the gods.
MID_EV11_030_m01_007: One day, I hope to duel you with this sword.
MID_EV11_030_m01_008: What? What do you mean? Why me? Oh. He's gone.
MID_EV11_030_m01_009: He's terrifying, but...he can't be all bad, right?
MID_EV11_030_m01_010: I beg your pardon. You are called Tialla, yes?
MID_EV11_030_m01_011: Y-yes. Did I overstep with you out there?
MID_EV11_030_m01_012: No. Your judgment was perspicacious. Your youth\ngave me cause to underestimate you.
MID_EV11_030_m01_013: Yet your mind is a precision instrument, and your\nknowledge exceeds your years.
MID_EV11_030_m01_014: It is only right that I acknowledge this, as ought\nwe all.
MID_EV11_030_m01_015: Th-thank you. This is...unexpected.
MID_EV11_030_m01_016: Do not misunderstand me. I am pleased to speak to\nany who have demonstrated their intelligence.
MID_EV11_030_m01_017: Perhaps one day we can face each other across a\ngame board and debate strategy.
MID_EV11_030_m01_018: Whoa! So it turns out you can be nice!
MID_EV11_030_m01_019: It is as I said. All whom I encounter are accorded the\nrespect their intellect dictates.
MID_EV11_030_m01_020: Well, that explains things! You think I'm stupid!\nAnd that's why you're always picking on me!
MID_EV11_030_m01_021: It is wonderful that you are so self-aware. Hmm?
MID_EV11_030_m01_034: Whoa! So it turns out you can be nice!
MID_EV11_030_m01_035: It is as I said. All whom I encounter are accorded the\nrespect their intellect dictates.
MID_EV11_030_m01_036: Well, that explains things! You think I'm stupid!\nAnd that's why you're always picking on me!
MID_EV11_030_m01_037: It is wonderful that you are so self-aware. Hmm?
MID_EV11_030_m01_022: We must speak. There is much to discuss, if you\nwould only grant me the time.
MID_EV11_030_m01_023: Rgh...
MID_EV11_030_m01_024: Anatolia! You were amazing out there!
MID_EV11_030_m01_025: My performance wasn't anything special. I'll be\nleaving now.
MID_EV11_030_m01_026: Apologies, Cai. I'll be heading out now too.
MID_EV11_030_m01_027: Hey, um, good luck out there! Keep on fighting the\ngood fight!
MID_EV11_030_m01_038: Hey, um, good luck out there! Keep on fighting the\ngood fight!
MID_EV11_030_m01_049: 
MID_EV11_030_m01_029: They're not worried about the impression they make!\nWell, neither is Sweetie...
MID_EV11_030_m01_030: About Anatolia and her friends... Did something\nhappen between you and them?
MID_EV11_030_m01_031: Me? I didn't say a word. Nope! Not a peep! You're\nimagining things. Right? Right. OK! Bye!
MID_EV11_030_m01_039: They're not worried about the impression they make!\nWell, neither is Sweetie...
MID_EV11_030_m01_040: About Anatolia and her friends... Did something\nhappen between you and them?
MID_EV11_030_m01_041: Me? I didn't say a word. Nope! Not a peep! You're\nimagining things. Right? Right. OK! Bye!
MID_EV11_030_m01_028: Why is everyone in such a rush?
MID_EV11_031_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_031_m01_001: So the youth wins again. It was a hard-won victory,\nI note.
MID_EV11_031_m01_002: Yes, it was a narrow thing. These children are not\nin serious contention.
MID_EV11_031_m01_003: I could personally overcome such paltry opposition\nbefore the count of 30.
MID_EV11_031_m01_004: Your Majesty would have made light work of\nthe battle, I agree.
MID_EV11_031_m01_005: Even should luck carry them through the qualifiers,\nthey will stumble early in the main bracket.
MID_EV11_031_m01_006: That is why I find it so unusual for Your Majesty\nto concern herself with these foreigners.
MID_EV11_031_m01_007: Foreigners who we may someday face as enemies,\nat that.
MID_EV11_031_m01_008: Have you developed a soft spot for the boy?
MID_EV11_031_m01_009: The jewel in his palm is a curiosity. But I am more\ninterested in the dark fencer and the white bride.
MID_EV11_031_m01_010: Those arrayed before us are formidable. Our path\nforward will be paved in bones.
MID_EV11_031_m01_011: Oho! I don't much care for the sound of that. Not if\nit puts Your Majesty in such a dark mood.
MID_EV11_031_m01_012: Worry not. We Saraminians have a long-held dream\nthat we will abandon for no one.
MID_EV11_031_m01_013: Their own causes and concerns matter not. Yet I do\npity them.
MID_EV11_031_m01_014: They, like us, have invested greatly in seizing this\nunique opportunity.
MID_EV11_031_m01_015: But I will allow no one else to claim the prize that is\nrightly ours.